[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) Integration in Selenium"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Chrome DevTools Protocol allows for more advanced control and inspection of Chromium-based browsers beyond standard WebDriver capabilities. Selenium 4 provides native support for CDP, empowering automation engineers to intercept network traffic, mock geolocation, override device metrics, and more."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Selenium 4.x or higher (which natively implements CDP support)."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A Chromium-based browser (Chrome, Microsoft Edge, etc.)."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Appropriate driver binaries compatible with your browser version."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Initializing the DevTools Session"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"To use CDP features in Java with Selenium, you need to cast your WebDriver instance to a HasDevTools interface and create a DevTools session."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"ChromeDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
DevTools devTools = driver.getDevTools();
devTools.createSession();"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Example 1: Emulating Network Conditions"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can use CDP to simulate slow network speeds, such as 3G or offline modes, to test how your web application handles poor connectivity."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"devTools.send(Network.enable(Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty()));
devTools.send(Network.emulateNetworkConditions(
    false,
    100.0,
    200000,
    100000,
    Optional.of(Network.ConnectionType.CELLULAR3G)
));"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Example 2: Overriding Geolocation"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Testing location-based features often requires spoofing GPS coordinates. CDP enables you to override geolocation parameters seamlessly."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"devTools.send(Emulation.setGeolocationOverride(
    Optional.of(37.7749),
    Optional.of(-122.4194),
    Optional.of(1)
));"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"Integrating CDP into your Selenium scripts opens up endless possibilities for advanced browser manipulation and robust testing scenarios that were previously impossible with WebDriver alone."}]
